WEBVTT

00:02.560 --> 00:06.690
This is sugoroku that you don't need
to roll dice to advance, isn't it?

00:07.070 --> 00:09.040
Card strategy sugoroku, huh?

00:09.040 --> 00:12.820
I have no experience with this game either,
so this is an even contest.

00:14.800 --> 00:18.210
This is a game that requires four players.

00:18.210 --> 00:22.260
All right! Let me show you my partner
from our team, "Tempest Cruiser"!

00:22.730 --> 00:23.920
I shall be your opponent.

00:26.370 --> 00:28.140
I'm Kelritch Shee.

00:28.140 --> 00:29.880
I'm Dax's subordinate.

00:29.880 --> 00:33.600
Now, Fay!
You should choose your partner!

00:33.600 --> 00:36.600
I knew you'd choose
the former dragon, Leoleshea, right?!

00:37.020 --> 00:38.380
You can do it, right?

00:39.130 --> 00:42.190
I'm not afraid of games anymore!

00:42.860 --> 00:47.150
I'll cheer you two from my seat.
So do your best, okay?

00:47.150 --> 00:48.630
Y-Yes!

00:53.660 --> 00:58.200
PLAYER.06: MIND ARENA

01:01.630 --> 01:04.400
Mind Arena has two conditions for victory:

01:04.880 --> 01:08.690
Either the player must reach
the goal four squares away first,

01:08.690 --> 01:13.040
or the player must use a Trap or Magic card
to reduce the enemy team's life from 20

01:13.040 --> 01:15.220
to zero at the end of the turn.

01:15.710 --> 01:16.960
HEALER: +1 LIFE RESTORED WHEN USING HEALING MAGIC
In order to win,

01:16.960 --> 01:19.250
WIZARD: +1 DAMAGE WHEN USING ATTACK MAGIC
you will be asked to choose a class.

01:19.250 --> 01:20.240
TRAVELER: MAY ADD +1 SQUARE
The classes that have simple abilities are

01:20.240 --> 01:21.270
WHEN USING A DICE CARD.
The classes that have simple abilities are

01:21.270 --> 01:23.130
(UP TO A MAXIMUM OF 7 SQUARES' MOVEMENT)
the "Wizard" class, which specializes in attack,

01:23.130 --> 01:23.910
TRAPPER: TRAP SQUARES
and the "Healer" class in healing.

01:23.910 --> 01:24.840
DO NOT AFFECT PLAYERS WITH THIS CLASS.
and the "Healer" class in healing.

01:24.840 --> 01:26.890
IN ADDITION, TRAP SQUARES THEY LAND ON
"Traveler" and "Trapper" classes

01:26.890 --> 01:29.240
ARE STRENGTHENED
seem to be more versatile.

01:29.240 --> 01:32.780
Before the class selection,
five Magic cards will be randomly

01:32.780 --> 01:34.240
distributed to each player.

01:34.650 --> 01:37.050
Amazing.
They show up right in front of us.

01:37.050 --> 01:42.210
There are three main types of Magic cards:
"Attack," "Recovery," and "Special."

01:42.210 --> 01:43.210
For example,

01:43.210 --> 01:45.660
MEGA FLAME: HIGH-SPEED MAGIC CARD
the attack magic "Mega Flame"

01:45.660 --> 01:49.150
DEALS 2 DAMAGE TO ONE OPPONENT PLAYER
can deal 2 damage to the opponent player.

01:49.150 --> 01:53.180
And the used cards are stored
in each team's storage.

01:53.630 --> 01:56.140
There are 72 Magic cards in total.

01:56.140 --> 01:59.980
The information on the cards
can be accessed at any time.

01:59.980 --> 02:05.610
I see. This is a head-to-head battle
in which all card data is disclosed.

02:06.380 --> 02:08.170
This is a 'Secret Card.'

02:08.170 --> 02:10.690
You have to choose
the Healer class to use it.

02:11.100 --> 02:13.670
I have a rare Magic card here...

02:15.090 --> 02:17.290
"Can only be activated
when your life is 5 or less

02:17.290 --> 02:20.370
and you have 1 card in your hand."

02:20.370 --> 02:23.220
The conditions are pretty tricky to use.

02:23.220 --> 02:25.590
It has an interesting effect, but...

02:28.950 --> 02:33.010
However, the first thing
we have to decide is our class.

02:33.430 --> 02:36.730
The Traveler advances a lot,
and the Healer protects your life.

02:36.730 --> 02:38.430
In other words, these two classes...

02:38.430 --> 02:41.280
The classes that aim
to last long enough to finish the game.

02:41.280 --> 02:44.940
The opposites are Wizard and Trapper.

02:44.940 --> 02:47.650
Both are classes that deal
damage to the opponent.

02:48.020 --> 02:52.170
But our hand is overwhelmingly
filled with Recovery magic,

02:52.170 --> 02:55.180
so it's hard to reduce their life to zero.

02:55.180 --> 02:57.430
Are we using a pattern
like royal sugoroku

02:57.430 --> 02:59.730
to reach the goal and win?

03:04.230 --> 03:09.190
I don't think I'm going to choose
to stall the game plan.

03:12.260 --> 03:14.280
It's time to start the game.

03:14.280 --> 03:16.220
Please choose your class.

03:20.540 --> 03:21.640
I accept your challenge!

03:22.080 --> 03:23.140
I choose...

03:23.590 --> 03:24.600
...the Traveler class!

03:33.780 --> 03:35.570
And I choose Healer!

03:40.070 --> 03:41.780
I'll choose "Wizard"!

03:42.860 --> 03:44.700
And I also choose "Wizard".

03:47.460 --> 03:49.510
They both chose Wizard class?

03:49.510 --> 03:52.380
So they're focusing strictly
on firepower to reduce our lives.

03:52.810 --> 03:55.090
Next, the dice cards will be distributed.

03:58.050 --> 04:00.640
So this is what they use instead of dice.

04:01.010 --> 04:06.380
All players may choose
any number of dice cards from 1-6.

04:06.380 --> 04:09.510
GOLDEN SQUARE: DRAW 2 MAGIC CARDS
Golden squares draw two Magic cards.

04:09.510 --> 04:11.270
Silver squares draw one Magic card.

04:11.270 --> 04:13.550
SILVER SQUARE: DRAW 1 MAGIC CARD
Silver squares draw one Magic card.

04:13.550 --> 04:15.470
Red squares become trap zones

04:15.470 --> 04:18.740
RED SQUARE: TRAP ZONE THAT DEALS 7 DAMAGE
that give 7 unmitigable damage.

04:20.700 --> 04:24.050
Choosing 6 is the fastest way
to the finish line,

04:24.050 --> 04:27.570
but if we stop at the same square,
we cannot draw a card.

04:27.910 --> 04:31.760
The choice is to aim for the goal
or to make full use of the cards.

04:31.760 --> 04:35.380
This game demands a tactical game
right from the start.

04:36.050 --> 04:37.410
That's right.

04:37.840 --> 04:39.800
Beginning Phase 1.

04:39.800 --> 04:43.040
All players, place your dice cards
face down on the field.

04:43.810 --> 04:46.240
Pearl, we're going to go first!

04:46.240 --> 04:47.540
Y-Yes!

04:52.220 --> 04:54.590
Now, game begins.

04:56.690 --> 04:59.520
The turn goes to the player
with the highest number of eyes.

04:59.520 --> 05:02.050
However, in the case of duplicate numbers,

05:02.050 --> 05:05.060
the player who chooses
the first number goes first.

05:05.060 --> 05:08.410
Thus, the order is Fay, Dax, and so on.

05:11.640 --> 05:12.800
My turn!

05:17.910 --> 05:21.470
Normally, he could draw a Magic card here...

05:21.470 --> 05:24.470
But since Dax is also in the same square,
he cannot draw a card.

05:25.760 --> 05:27.930
Fay, let me ask you something.

05:27.930 --> 05:30.300
Are you sure about that spot?

05:30.770 --> 05:32.300
What do you mean?

05:32.300 --> 05:33.630
Don't play dumb.

05:33.630 --> 05:35.990
The Traveler class
can choose one more square

05:35.990 --> 05:37.590
and go to the seventh square.

05:37.590 --> 05:40.240
I'm not using my Traveler ability now.

05:40.680 --> 05:44.950
So you wanted to land on
square 6 to rob me of my draw, huh?

05:44.950 --> 05:48.850
Operator, is it acceptable to trade
the Magic cards with our pair?

05:48.850 --> 05:50.480
No, it is not allowed.

05:50.480 --> 05:54.300
In addition, there is something similar
to swapping your Magic cards.

05:54.300 --> 05:55.420
All right.

05:59.190 --> 06:00.590
I end my turn.

06:00.590 --> 06:02.060
My turn!

06:06.580 --> 06:09.970
Then I'll use Wizard class's Secret Card!

06:10.990 --> 06:13.560
The highest level of rarity
among all the cards?!

06:14.050 --> 06:17.520
I cast the barrier spell,
Burning Rythm!

06:19.190 --> 06:21.990
BURNING RYTHM

06:21.990 --> 06:24.820
BURNING RYTHM
This card affects all players.

06:24.820 --> 06:26.900
BURNING RYTHM
This effect is a double-edged sword.

06:26.900 --> 06:28.780
WIZARD CLASS' EXCLUSIVE SECRET CARD
So if I'm attacked,

06:28.780 --> 06:31.450
WIZARD CLASS' EXCLUSIVE SECRET CARD
I take an equal amount of additional damage.

06:31.450 --> 06:33.910
But why would you use that card?

06:33.910 --> 06:35.670
I conclude my turn.

06:36.580 --> 06:38.980
It's my turn next, then!

06:44.050 --> 06:46.190
I'll save my cards, too.

06:46.190 --> 06:47.550
I end my turn!

06:47.550 --> 06:49.260
Then, my turn.

06:52.010 --> 06:53.640
I draw two cards.

06:54.360 --> 06:56.690
I cast Twin Bolt.

06:56.690 --> 07:00.190
Fay, Pearl, I deal 1 damage to each of you!

07:13.540 --> 07:17.920
Dax's secret card, Burning Rythm,
is no joke.

07:18.460 --> 07:19.980
Twin Bolt deals 1 damage,

07:19.980 --> 07:22.420
and then Wizard class gives
an additional 1 damage.

07:22.930 --> 07:27.100
Each attack adds 1 damage
from the Burning Rythm

07:27.100 --> 07:28.760
and makes a total of 4 damage.

07:29.220 --> 07:32.930
Since this Burning Rhythm
effect will continue,

07:32.930 --> 07:37.140
are we going to lose our lives at this rate?

07:37.650 --> 07:40.800
If we keep taking this damage,
we will be wiped out.

07:41.480 --> 07:43.900
I still have 38 squares to reach the goal,

07:43.900 --> 07:45.570
and you have 40 squares.

07:45.570 --> 07:48.780
Even if we move 6 squares each turn,
it will take 7 turns to reach the goal.

07:49.360 --> 07:53.660
Fay, your objective is to reach
the goal as fast as possible.

07:53.660 --> 07:55.370
In contrast, Kelritch and I

07:55.370 --> 07:58.600
are going to destroy you as fast as possible
with our maximum firepower!

07:58.600 --> 08:00.430
My turn isn't over.

08:00.430 --> 08:01.530
I cast a barrier,

08:01.530 --> 08:03.880
Chains of Malice.

08:07.760 --> 08:13.100
CHAINS OF MALICE: SELF-APPLIED MAGIC CARD

08:16.140 --> 08:18.480
B-Barrier magic?!

08:18.850 --> 08:21.190
I end my turn.

08:21.850 --> 08:23.640
We're after one thing.

08:24.060 --> 08:25.910
So we can't let them notice it.

08:26.630 --> 08:28.650
We'll use our cards without hesitation.

08:28.650 --> 08:33.020
If we save them up,
those two Wizards will burn up our lives.

08:33.020 --> 08:34.540
I-I agree!

08:34.990 --> 08:37.000
Beginning Phase 2.

08:37.000 --> 08:40.330
All players, place your dice cards
face down on the field.

08:41.250 --> 08:43.210
Don't hesitate, Pearl! Use them!

08:43.530 --> 08:44.510
Yes!

08:45.170 --> 08:47.820
Now, opening the dice cards.

08:49.260 --> 08:51.760
Are you trying to prevent me
from getting more cards?

08:51.760 --> 08:53.410
O-Of course!

08:53.410 --> 08:56.290
I knew you'd go for the golden square!

08:56.650 --> 08:59.640
And my High-Speed Magic, Pearl Fire!

09:00.060 --> 09:01.600
Pearl... Fire?

09:01.930 --> 09:06.070
High-Speed Magic is a useful magic that
can be used during the opponent's turn.

09:06.070 --> 09:08.390
No, I know that,

09:08.390 --> 09:10.280
but what I want to know is the name...

09:12.110 --> 09:13.150
MEGA FLAME: HIGH-SPEED MAGIC CARD

09:13.150 --> 09:14.910
MEGA FLAME: HIGH-SPEED MAGIC CARD
That's not the card you said it was!

09:14.910 --> 09:19.620
"Mega Flame" is a dumb name,
and I could never be happy using it!

09:19.620 --> 09:22.040
So, there you have it: Pearl Fire!

09:25.350 --> 09:27.090
Attack Dax!

09:30.590 --> 09:33.670
How's that? The usual Mega Flame
only deals 2 damage,

09:33.670 --> 09:35.430
but now it's 3 because I changed its name!

09:35.430 --> 09:38.750
You'll get extra damage
from Burning Rhythm, you know?

09:41.140 --> 09:45.110
These two Barrier Magics are too tricky!

09:45.110 --> 09:47.000
Because this is the Secret Card.

09:47.000 --> 09:51.360
Pearl, I'm going to return
all the pain you've caused me!

09:54.750 --> 09:57.490
I cast Dax Thunder!

09:57.490 --> 10:00.340
The official name is "Blizzard."

10:00.340 --> 10:03.960
Maybe it's a counter to the Pearl Fire
she mentioned earlier...

10:03.960 --> 10:08.560
I'm surprised you had the audacity
to name a card after yourself!

10:08.560 --> 10:11.920
I commend you
on your exceptional idea!

10:11.920 --> 10:13.470
That's what I'm talking about!

10:13.470 --> 10:15.260
He's competing with her now...

10:15.260 --> 10:18.240
Take this, Dax Thunder!

10:24.330 --> 10:26.240
Where's the 'thunder'?

10:27.130 --> 10:31.420
We're only on Phase 2,
but we've already cornered...

10:31.420 --> 10:32.650
Cornered?

10:32.650 --> 10:35.110
You're too naive!
I'll end this right now!

10:40.240 --> 10:43.010
I cast SELF-APPLIED MAGIC,
Crash of the Heavens.

10:45.220 --> 10:47.210
Instead of receiving 4 damage, including

10:47.210 --> 10:49.320
the card cost of Chains of Malice and Rhythm,

10:49.320 --> 10:51.280
the opponent receives 4 damage.

10:51.280 --> 10:54.590
Combined with my Wizard ability
and Burning Rythm, the total is 7 damage.

10:54.590 --> 10:57.930
Pearl, you have one life remaining.

10:57.930 --> 11:01.640
I have High-Speed Recovery Magic,
Hope in Abundance!

11:01.950 --> 11:04.700
By storing one card
from my hand to storage,

11:04.700 --> 11:06.530
I can nullify up to 8 damage!

11:07.230 --> 11:10.440
And since I'm a healer,
that makes it 9—

11:10.440 --> 11:11.530
You fell for it.

11:11.530 --> 11:12.360
Huh?

11:12.360 --> 11:15.070
High-Speed Magic, Price of Greed!

11:17.070 --> 11:19.500
I can nullify my opponent's recovery magic!

11:20.530 --> 11:25.060
Now that my 7 damage remains,
there goes your 1 life.

11:25.060 --> 11:27.560
Further, you activated Hope in Abundance,

11:27.560 --> 11:31.190
which triggered Chains of Malice,
and you'll lose 2 points of life.

11:31.500 --> 11:33.610
Don't forget about me!

11:33.610 --> 11:35.970
High-Speed Magic, Bandaged Heart!

11:36.720 --> 11:39.680
Reduce damage to a player by 2!

11:39.680 --> 11:41.640
He still have a card to counter?

11:41.640 --> 11:45.730
Fay, helping your friend here
means hurting yourself.

11:45.730 --> 11:48.940
We'll see about that.
My turn!

11:49.640 --> 11:52.860
By using the damage I just took from
Chain of Malice as the trigger,

11:53.400 --> 11:55.860
I cast Attack Magic,
Sword of the Heavenly Army!

11:56.540 --> 11:59.490
Dax, you will take a total of 5 damage!

11:59.490 --> 12:00.950
What?

12:00.950 --> 12:03.180
And I use one more Self-Applied Magic,

12:03.180 --> 12:05.160
Soul's Sacrifice this turn.

12:05.160 --> 12:08.620
By removing an unnecessary
card from my hand,

12:08.620 --> 12:11.630
I recover 3 life points for both of us.

12:11.970 --> 12:13.150
I end my turn.

12:13.150 --> 12:15.030
Then it's my turn!

12:17.840 --> 12:22.830
I cast 2 cards of Water of Oasis
to recover 10 life points.

12:23.760 --> 12:25.310
And I end my turn.

12:25.630 --> 12:28.630
It looks like Dax is running out
of life points.

12:28.630 --> 12:31.300
He is saving six cards in his hand.

12:32.200 --> 12:33.800
Beginning Phase 3.

12:33.800 --> 12:37.330
All players, place your dice cards
face down on the field.

12:39.910 --> 12:42.870
Fay, I'll seize the victory in this phase!

12:43.200 --> 12:46.290
Pearl, we're going
the winning route as we planned!

12:46.610 --> 12:48.280
Right to the bitter end!

12:48.280 --> 12:49.450
Of course!

12:50.360 --> 12:53.000
Now, opening the dice cards.

12:54.340 --> 12:55.910
Dax chose 4?!

12:55.910 --> 12:57.550
Hey, that square...

12:58.670 --> 13:02.450
Four squares ahead of Dax
is a trap square.

13:02.450 --> 13:06.140
Is he going to step on the trap
on purpose to take 7 damage?

13:07.610 --> 13:08.480
But first...

13:08.990 --> 13:10.100
My turn.

13:11.990 --> 13:13.560
I draw two cards

13:13.560 --> 13:16.900
and discard one to use this card.

13:17.300 --> 13:19.330
Super Magic, Pearl Barrier.

13:20.610 --> 13:24.140
I can nullify one of the next
magic spells that targets me.

13:24.570 --> 13:25.830
I end my turn.

13:25.830 --> 13:27.530
Then, my turn!

13:29.110 --> 13:33.080
I use the ability of Traveler to add
1 square and advance 7 squares.

13:33.700 --> 13:34.960
I end my turn.

13:34.960 --> 13:38.370
Are you both wary of us
and trying to save your cards?

13:38.370 --> 13:42.690
Pearl, your magic was a good choice,

13:42.690 --> 13:44.430
but it is still not enough.

13:46.640 --> 13:48.600
It doesn't matter how careful you are,

13:48.600 --> 13:50.980
our victory is assured.

13:51.620 --> 13:53.940
I cast Mega Flame.

13:53.940 --> 13:55.900
You're using my Pearl Fire?!

13:55.900 --> 13:57.530
This is Mega Flame.

13:57.530 --> 13:59.610
The target is you, of course.

14:02.950 --> 14:06.830
I knew you would do that,
so I cast Pearl Barrier!

14:10.410 --> 14:12.920
That is also in my calculation.

14:12.920 --> 14:16.150
Here, I cast 'Absolute Resource Equality.'

14:18.800 --> 14:22.860
All players must draw
or discard their cards

14:22.860 --> 14:25.800
until they have four cards in their hands.

14:26.550 --> 14:28.140
What are you planning?

14:28.140 --> 14:32.100
You are all free to draw cards
until you have four cards.

14:35.000 --> 14:38.480
And finally, I set up this Timed Magic.

14:38.840 --> 14:39.870
I conclude my turn.

14:42.270 --> 14:43.650
My turn.

14:47.370 --> 14:50.890
You might think there's no advantage
to this square, right?

14:50.890 --> 14:54.140
But by using the High-Speed Magic,
Double Trap,

14:54.140 --> 14:56.580
I can change the target of the damage!

14:56.580 --> 14:58.150
I figured that would come!

14:58.150 --> 15:00.180
There is no way
you would step on the trap

15:00.180 --> 15:02.800
except to cause damage to someone else!

15:02.800 --> 15:05.240
This damage cannot be mitigated.

15:05.240 --> 15:07.020
Pearl's life is 8,

15:07.020 --> 15:09.680
and the damage from the trap is 7,

15:09.680 --> 15:12.980
and with the effect of
Burning Rhythm, becomes 8!

15:16.770 --> 15:18.230
Not so fast!

15:18.230 --> 15:20.940
High-Speed Magic,
A Twin's Agony!

15:23.900 --> 15:26.510
So you had the right card
for that moment, huh?

15:26.510 --> 15:29.620
But I've been waiting for you
to cast the card!

15:29.620 --> 15:30.830
What?!

15:30.830 --> 15:33.720
I cast Self-Applied Magic,
Order of Silence!

15:34.290 --> 15:38.660
I can seal all your cards
until the end of this phase!

15:38.660 --> 15:40.170
I end my turn!

15:40.480 --> 15:41.380
Fay!

15:41.380 --> 15:42.820
Calm down, Pearl.

15:42.820 --> 15:45.500
Your cards are not sealed.

15:45.500 --> 15:47.840
And Phase 3 is already over!

15:47.840 --> 15:48.860
No.

15:48.860 --> 15:53.060
I open my Timed Magic
when all players have finished their turns.

15:55.520 --> 15:57.440
DESTINY

15:57.440 --> 15:58.500
AT THE END OF THE PHASE,

15:58.500 --> 16:00.730
ALL PLAYERS TAKE DAMAGE EQUAL
TO THE NUMBER OF CARDS THEY DREW

16:00.730 --> 16:02.230
IF A PLAYER DREW 4 OR MORE CARDS,
THEY TAKE 10 DAMAGE

16:02.230 --> 16:04.940
Can Master Fay and Pearl be saved?

16:04.940 --> 16:05.840
No.

16:07.970 --> 16:09.660
You seem to have realized this.

16:09.660 --> 16:13.090
This is the real reason
I let you draw four cards.

16:13.090 --> 16:15.080
It's all part of the plan.

16:15.580 --> 16:17.790
You have 5 life points left,

16:17.790 --> 16:20.220
and this magic is going to do 10 damage.

16:20.220 --> 16:22.880
Will your recovery magic
be enough to stop it?

16:27.420 --> 16:29.840
Then, this is our victory.

16:40.690 --> 16:44.280
I'm not a burden to Fay and the others!

16:44.740 --> 16:47.780
This turn isn't over yet!
I won't let it be!

16:48.800 --> 16:50.450
I cast 'Last Dance'!

16:50.450 --> 16:52.960
LAST DANCE: HIGH-SPEED MAGIC CARD
It can only be used when your life total

16:52.960 --> 16:54.200
LAST DANCE: HIGH-SPEED MAGIC CARD
would otherwise be zero!

16:54.200 --> 16:55.160
What?

16:55.160 --> 16:56.370
That's...!

16:56.370 --> 16:58.930
A strong card has a great risk.

16:58.930 --> 17:02.970
At the end of this additional turn,
I take 20 damage,

17:02.970 --> 17:04.820
and my defeat is confirmed.

17:05.340 --> 17:07.500
I am not afraid of losing.

17:07.500 --> 17:10.800
If I keep running away from the game,
nothing will change!

17:11.370 --> 17:12.790
A dirty little trick!

17:15.720 --> 17:17.760
I've finished passing the baton to Pearl.

17:18.770 --> 17:20.440
All that's left is to believe

17:20.440 --> 17:22.270
in the partner I've chosen.

17:23.140 --> 17:25.090
This is my final turn!

17:28.710 --> 17:31.700
First, I cast my Self-Applied Magic,
Life Pulse!

17:31.700 --> 17:35.410
If my remaining life total is 3 or less,
I will recover 10 life points.

17:35.410 --> 17:38.680
I have 1 life and 4 cards in my hand.

17:38.680 --> 17:40.400
I'll attack you

17:40.980 --> 17:43.380
with 4 life points remaining!

17:49.970 --> 17:52.660
My first card is Counterbolt!

17:54.030 --> 17:57.140
It deals 5 damage with the effect
Burning Rythm makes for 6 damage!

17:57.140 --> 17:58.520
Then I...

17:59.220 --> 18:03.100
I'll use my High-Speed Magic,
First Aid, to reduce the damage!

18:03.100 --> 18:05.060
Next, Pearl Fire!

18:05.060 --> 18:07.130
If this magic reaches you, I win!

18:10.680 --> 18:12.480
Did you forget about me?

18:12.480 --> 18:15.870
I use High-Speed magic, Saint's Charity,
to recover our life points.

18:16.340 --> 18:18.560
I use two cards to heal us.

18:18.560 --> 18:21.830
Dax's life point is 3, and mine is 14.

18:21.830 --> 18:24.170
I already figured
that you have recovery magic!

18:24.590 --> 18:26.020
Ancient Word!

18:26.020 --> 18:27.590
ANCIENT WORD
It dealt damage equal

18:27.590 --> 18:28.710
ANCIENT WORD
the total cards I've played,

18:28.710 --> 18:30.460
which means 3!

18:31.940 --> 18:35.890
With Burning Rythm effect, it deals
7 damage! That means we win!

18:38.280 --> 18:40.270
That was brilliant gameplay.

18:40.880 --> 18:42.560
What is that attitude?!

18:42.960 --> 18:46.320
I couldn't have imagined that you would
be so aggressive all by yourself.

18:46.730 --> 18:48.930
You're not a burden to Fay,

18:49.440 --> 18:51.150
but you're one step ahead of him.

18:51.490 --> 18:53.900
High-Speed Magic, Karmic Cycle!

18:54.720 --> 18:58.030
All the damage I take will be
transferred to Kelritch!

19:05.110 --> 19:06.580
I survive.

19:06.580 --> 19:10.170
And you take 20 damage
from the Last Dance.

19:10.700 --> 19:11.900
You lose.

19:16.020 --> 19:20.180
I'm sorry. I tried my best to win
without relying on you, Fay.

19:20.180 --> 19:22.060
But I'm not quite experienced enough yet.

19:22.060 --> 19:25.330
What are you talking about? We won.

19:25.330 --> 19:27.770
You're the best partner, Pearl.

19:30.230 --> 19:32.820
W-What are you talking about?

19:32.820 --> 19:34.800
My last card...

19:35.980 --> 19:38.430
I finally met the activation condition.

19:39.220 --> 19:40.900
The last remaining card...

19:40.900 --> 19:41.700
This is

19:42.150 --> 19:43.910
a card that calls to other cards!

19:44.960 --> 19:47.670
I cast High-Speed Magic, Encore!

19:47.670 --> 19:52.680
It allows me to add one card that's been
stored to the storage to my hand!

19:53.360 --> 19:55.850
I have a rare Magic card here...

19:57.290 --> 19:59.460
"Can only be activated
when your life is 5 or less

19:59.460 --> 20:02.640
and you have 1 card in your hand."

20:02.640 --> 20:05.450
The conditions are pretty tricky to use.

20:07.080 --> 20:09.690
Now, it's time to compare answers!

20:09.690 --> 20:12.580
The card I chose from the storage

20:12.580 --> 20:14.310
is the Healer's Secret Card!

20:14.690 --> 20:16.090
Heartache!

20:17.030 --> 20:19.990
That's ridiculous!
Why did you have that Secret Card?!

20:22.140 --> 20:24.080
How can a card
that has never been used

20:24.080 --> 20:26.830
in this game be stored in storage?

20:26.830 --> 20:28.660
Did everyone forget?

20:28.660 --> 20:34.090
Fey sent an unused card
to storage in Phase 2, right?

20:34.090 --> 20:37.800
Ah! When Master Fay
used Soul's Sacrifice!

20:38.270 --> 20:41.550
By removing an unnecessary card
from my hand...

20:42.090 --> 20:45.640
Fay, who chose the Traveler class,
knew it was a dead card.

20:46.050 --> 20:48.640
So he had to give it to Pearl,
the Healer class,

20:48.640 --> 20:51.020
as a trump card.

20:51.440 --> 20:55.230
Don't tell me... The question in Phase 1
was anticipation for this?

20:55.580 --> 20:58.200
Yeah, of course I was going for it.

20:58.560 --> 21:02.240
Operator, is it acceptable to trade
the Magic cards with our pair?

21:02.240 --> 21:04.040
Everything was a bluff.

21:04.040 --> 21:09.190
That question made everyone realize that
you had no way to trade cards in your hand.

21:09.580 --> 21:11.790
I just needed you guys
to let your guard down.

21:11.790 --> 21:14.910
And the reason I used the Sword
of the Heavenly Army right before that

21:14.910 --> 21:16.870
was just to get you looking somewhere else

21:16.870 --> 21:19.360
before I stored my card in the storage.

21:20.840 --> 21:22.250
I can't believe this...

21:22.880 --> 21:25.140
I said right when we chose
our classes, right?

21:25.610 --> 21:27.220
"I accept your challenge!"

21:30.640 --> 21:34.540
We were after damage from the start.

21:34.540 --> 21:36.810
Then why not just choose Wizard class?!

21:36.810 --> 21:39.820
Our hand had a definite bias
toward recovery magic.

21:39.820 --> 21:42.640
We would lose in a simple damage game,

21:42.640 --> 21:45.160
so we had to outwit you
with a mind game.

21:45.160 --> 21:47.170
This finally settles it!

21:47.620 --> 21:49.480
I cast Heartache!

21:49.480 --> 21:51.120
And I end my turn!

21:51.120 --> 21:54.430
I transfer 20 damage
from The Last Dance!

22:03.820 --> 22:05.150
I forfeit.

22:06.520 --> 22:08.890
It seems I was still taking you too lightly.

22:09.600 --> 22:10.750
Well played,

22:11.150 --> 22:12.760
Pearl Diamond.

22:21.070 --> 22:22.910
Dax's remaining life is zero.

22:22.910 --> 22:26.530
Fay and Pearl are the winners.

22:37.940 --> 22:42.130
I knew you and I are destined
to be rivals all our lives!

22:42.630 --> 22:43.590
Say what?

22:44.070 --> 22:47.070
Our battle today is
the beginning of destiny!

22:47.070 --> 22:50.570
The beginning of the legend of
the game, which shall be forged

22:50.570 --> 22:52.930
over tens of thousands of games
between you and me!

22:53.350 --> 22:54.570
Ah...

22:55.150 --> 22:57.470
Therefore, spectators!

22:57.470 --> 23:01.430
I promise you that I will overcome
this battle and become even stronger!

23:01.430 --> 23:04.360
My legend begins here!

23:12.320 --> 23:13.500
You did your best.

23:14.850 --> 23:16.320
Ah, no...

23:16.320 --> 23:17.960
I didn't do anything.

23:18.640 --> 23:19.920
Umm...

23:21.880 --> 23:25.220
Don't you think the losing side
is more excited?

23:28.750 --> 23:30.160
Well, that's fine.

23:30.160 --> 23:32.340
That means they enjoy the game.
